He's such a smart-mouth.

2310
01:06:12,160 --> 01:06:13,280
She's super chatty now too.

2311
01:06:13,920 --> 01:06:15,160
He's rubbing off on me.

2312
01:06:15,440 --> 01:06:17,320
That's a good thing.

2313
01:06:20,520 --> 01:06:21,720
He's just so cheeky!

2314
01:06:21,720 --> 01:06:22,280
So annoying!

2315
01:06:22,280 --> 01:06:23,760
I think he's corrupted Si!

2316
01:06:23,760 --> 01:06:24,200
Seriously.

2317
01:06:24,200 --> 01:06:25,680
Every time I see him, I wanna punch him!

2318
01:06:25,680 --> 01:06:26,480
Want me to help?

2319
01:06:26,480 --> 01:06:26,840
Sure.

2320
01:06:27,640 --> 01:06:28,000
Sure.

2321
01:06:28,000 --> 01:06:28,520
I'll help you!

2322
01:06:28,520 --> 01:06:29,520
I'm covered in bruises, Jingke!

2323
01:06:29,520 --> 01:06:30,650
(Joking)
I'm covered in bruises now!

2324
01:06:30,680 --> 01:06:31,400
Bruises everywhere!

2325
01:06:32,660 --> 01:06:33,160
(Playfully punches)

2326
01:06:33,160 --> 01:06:33,680
Take that.

2327
01:06:34,640 --> 01:06:35,320
Here's another.

2328
01:06:35,820 --> 01:06:37,140
(Acts cute)

2329
01:06:38,360 --> 01:06:39,360
Oh my goodness!

2330
01:06:43,740 --> 01:06:44,660
(Makes eye contact)

2331
01:06:46,120 --> 01:06:47,140
(Pinches)
Want some water?

2332
01:06:48,000 --> 01:06:49,440
Are you so nervous you need water?

2333
01:06:49,440 --> 01:06:49,920
No.

2334
01:06:50,400 --> 01:06:51,200
Which one do you want?

2335
01:06:54,360 --> 01:06:55,200
Having a private chat?

2336
01:06:55,200 --> 01:06:56,440
Yeah, I was telling him

2337
01:06:56,440 --> 01:06:58,680
that at the beginning,

2338
01:06:58,680 --> 01:07:00,120
he seemed really mature.

2339
01:07:00,120 --> 01:07:01,320
So we had

2340
01:07:01,320 --> 01:07:03,240
high expectations
of how he'd handle love.

2341
01:07:04,640 --> 01:07:06,160
But later, we realized

2342
01:07:06,160 --> 01:07:07,400
you're all still so young.

2343
01:07:07,720 --> 01:07:10,800
And there's really
no right or wrong in love.

2344
01:07:11,960 --> 01:07:13,160
True. I think relationships

2345
01:07:13,160 --> 01:07:14,840
can't be judged as right or wrong.

2346
01:07:15,040 --> 01:07:16,880
If they actually sent us
on the show to date,

2347
01:07:16,880 --> 01:07:17,920
we'd be just as clueless.

2348
01:07:21,120 --> 01:07:23,080
We sound so smart watching on TV,

2349
01:07:23,080 --> 01:07:24,120
giving all this advice.

2350
01:07:24,120 --> 01:07:24,800
But once we're in there,

2351
01:07:26,000 --> 01:07:27,400
we'd get all awkward

2352
01:07:27,400 --> 01:07:28,440
and shy!

2353
01:07:31,640 --> 01:07:32,520
By the time we're done being shy,

2354
01:07:32,520 --> 01:07:33,400
everyone's already dating!

2355
01:07:34,200 --> 01:07:35,040
We'd miss our chance!

2356
01:07:35,040 --> 01:07:36,920
Then go cry alone in our rooms, right?

2357
01:07:36,980 --> 01:07:38,860
(Feeling reassured)

2358
01:07:39,360 --> 01:07:40,960
I cried watching the confessions.

2359
01:07:40,960 --> 01:07:42,000
Those two made me cry.

2360
01:07:42,000 --> 01:07:42,880
But the second time you two did it,

2361
01:07:42,880 --> 01:07:44,040
I'd calmed down a little.

2362
01:07:44,560 --> 01:07:45,240
That first time, though...

2363
01:07:45,860 --> 01:07:47,120
(Tears streaming down)

2364
01:07:47,120 --> 01:07:48,240
At the confession spot?

2365
01:07:48,240 --> 01:07:48,800
Yeah.

2366
01:07:48,800 --> 01:07:50,960
All six of us watching

2367
01:07:50,960 --> 01:07:51,600
were bawling!

2368
01:07:52,000 --> 01:07:52,920
We had swollen eyes!

2369
01:07:53,360 --> 01:07:54,600
After Cui Kaiyi texted him,

2370
01:07:54,600 --> 01:07:55,840
he suddenly...

2371
01:07:55,840 --> 01:07:56,320
Exactly.

2372
01:07:56,320 --> 01:07:57,200
Became a different person.

2373
01:07:57,200 --> 01:07:57,760
You too.

2374
01:07:57,760 --> 01:07:58,560
You're both so brave.

2375
01:07:58,560 --> 01:07:59,560
Thank you.

2376
01:08:00,440 --> 01:08:01,960
So stay off social media.

2377
01:08:02,520 --> 01:08:03,880
Especially lately, okay?

2378
01:08:03,880 --> 01:08:05,520
Trust me. Just stay off social media.

2379
01:08:05,520 --> 01:08:06,560
If you don't check it,

2380
01:08:06,560 --> 01:08:07,880
after a while, if anything happens,

2381
01:08:07,880 --> 01:08:09,080
people close to you will tell you.

2382
01:08:09,080 --> 01:08:09,760
If my friends tell me something,

2383
01:08:09,760 --> 01:08:11,480
it's probably worth hearing.

2384
01:08:11,960 --> 01:08:12,640
So I'll listen.

2385
01:08:12,640 --> 01:08:13,960
Spend more time with friends.

2386
01:08:13,960 --> 01:08:15,120
Things like that.

2387
01:08:19,880 --> 01:08:20,920
Alright, everyone!

2388
01:08:20,920 --> 01:08:21,960
Let's eat!

2389
01:08:21,960 --> 01:08:24,120
Let's see who gets the first almond!

2390
01:08:24,140 --> 01:08:26,220
(Who'll find an almond?)

2391
01:08:26,240 --> 01:08:27,319
What kind of meat is this?

2392
01:08:29,080 --> 01:08:29,600
Celery.

2393
01:08:33,859 --> 01:08:34,779
(Thumbs up)

2394
01:08:34,800 --> 01:08:35,560
Delicious!

2395
01:08:35,960 --> 01:08:37,040
What's the filling? Try it.

2396
01:08:42,680 --> 01:08:43,760
The lamb filling's pretty good!

2397
01:08:47,760 --> 01:08:48,800
Here he comes!

2398
01:08:48,800 --> 01:08:49,680
Jingke's here!

2399
01:08:49,680 --> 01:08:51,000
Should I show everyone?

2400
01:08:51,000 --> 01:08:52,140
(Feeling a little shy)

2401
01:08:52,479 --> 01:08:53,760
Well, now I can say it too.

2402
01:08:53,760 --> 01:08:54,200
I'll be like...

2403
01:08:54,200 --> 01:08:54,979
(Found one!)

2404
01:08:55,180 --> 01:08:56,260
(Almond)

2405
01:08:57,600 --> 01:08:59,240
Give us your acceptance speech.

2406
01:08:59,240 --> 01:09:00,080
Acceptance speech?

2407
01:09:01,760 --> 01:09:02,720
I'm so lucky!

2408
01:09:02,720 --> 01:09:03,439
Thank you, everyone!

2409
01:09:05,319 --> 01:09:07,479
What was your happiest moment today?

2410
01:09:07,540 --> 01:09:08,100
(Curious)

2411
01:09:09,800 --> 01:09:11,000
Drawing that message.

2412
01:09:11,920 --> 01:09:14,560
Then why even consider long-distance?

2413
01:09:14,560 --> 01:09:16,060
(Then why even consider long-distance?)

2414
01:09:22,040 --> 01:09:22,800
Someone found one here too!

2415
01:09:22,960 --> 01:09:23,729
(Yihang finds an almond)
What a coincidence!

2416
01:09:24,360 --> 01:09:24,850
Almost broke my tooth!

2417
01:09:25,880 --> 01:09:27,600
Give us your acceptance speech!

2418
01:09:28,600 --> 01:09:30,279
Just getting to eat dumplings made by Si

2419
01:09:30,279 --> 01:09:31,319
makes me so lucky!

2420
01:09:34,160 --> 01:09:35,279
See how cheeky he is?

2421
01:09:35,279 --> 01:09:36,120
So cheeky.

2422
01:09:37,399 --> 01:09:38,439
We've got one too!

2423
01:09:38,439 --> 01:09:38,939
(Fang gets an almond dumpling)

2424
01:09:39,640 --> 01:09:41,279
You found one!

2425
01:09:41,760 --> 01:09:44,279
Thanks for feeding me this lucky almond.

2426
01:09:48,359 --> 01:09:51,560
I'm happy to feed you.

2427
01:09:54,840 --> 01:09:55,440
This one's got one!

2428
01:09:55,440 --> 01:09:57,080
(Cui Kaiyi gets an almond dumpling)

2429
01:09:57,080 --> 01:09:57,960
Cui Kaiyi got one too!

2430
01:09:58,320 --> 01:10:00,280
I'm grateful the Signal House

2431
01:10:00,280 --> 01:10:01,240
brought us all together.

2432
01:10:01,240 --> 01:10:01,840
And brought me such a wonderful...

2433
01:10:04,200 --> 01:10:05,160
Such a wonderful Cao Yiheng.

2434
01:10:08,440 --> 01:10:10,120
Nice!

2435
01:10:10,120 --> 01:10:11,080
Together forever!

2436
01:10:13,440 --> 01:10:14,640
(Zhao Xilun gets an almond dumpling)
I got one!

2437
01:10:14,680 --> 01:10:16,400
You got one!

2438
01:10:16,600 --> 01:10:17,760
I'm already lucky just being with you.

2439
01:10:21,960 --> 01:10:23,080
Nice.

2440
01:10:24,600 --> 01:10:26,200
(Bohan gets an almond dumpling)
I got one too!

2441
01:10:26,200 --> 01:10:27,280
Bohan found one too!

2442
01:10:27,280 --> 01:10:28,200
Bohan got one!

2443
01:10:28,400 --> 01:10:29,400
Xing's People, Lucky Ones.

2444
01:10:29,800 --> 01:10:30,810
Xing's People.

2445
01:10:30,840 --> 01:10:31,840
Xing's People, Lucky Ones.

2446
01:10:32,940 --> 01:10:34,060
(Glances)

2447
01:10:38,000 --> 01:10:38,880
Wrapping the dumplings with care

2448
01:10:38,880 --> 01:10:40,480
is like holding on to happiness.

2449
01:10:40,480 --> 01:10:40,760
Yeah.

2450
01:10:40,760 --> 01:10:42,000
One big, happy family.

2451
01:10:42,360 --> 01:10:43,360
We're all here

2452
01:10:43,880 --> 01:10:46,040
making dumplings together!

2453
01:10:46,040 --> 01:10:46,880
Great!

2454
01:10:48,120 --> 01:10:49,360
Now that afternoon tea's over,

2455
01:10:49,360 --> 01:10:50,840
let's get ready for dinner!

2456
01:10:50,840 --> 01:10:51,160
Let's go!

2457
01:10:56,160 --> 01:10:57,000
Let's go!

2458
01:10:57,200 --> 01:10:57,960
Easy!

2459
01:10:57,960 --> 01:10:58,440
No rush.

2460
01:10:58,440 --> 01:10:59,440
I'll get on this one.

2461
01:10:59,440 --> 01:11:00,240
Careful!

2462
01:11:01,000 --> 01:11:02,160
Let me do it.

2463
01:11:03,460 --> 01:11:04,340
(Holds hands)

2464
01:11:07,080 --> 01:11:07,840
Off we go!

2465
01:11:08,640 --> 01:11:09,320
Let's go!

2466
01:11:15,640 --> 01:11:16,600
It's pretty well-behaved.

2467
01:11:16,780 --> 01:11:17,800
Super well-behaved.

2468
01:11:18,660 --> 01:11:19,300
(Reaches out)

2469
01:11:33,320 --> 01:11:34,560
So beautiful!

2470
01:11:34,560 --> 01:11:35,400
Wow!

2471
01:11:35,400 --> 01:11:36,360
This is gorgeous!

2472
01:11:37,880 --> 01:11:38,960
These grasslands are beautiful!

2473
01:11:38,960 --> 01:11:39,880
Absolutely gorgeous!

2474
01:11:40,160 --> 01:11:40,640
Yeah!

2475
01:11:41,080 --> 01:11:42,560
This feels amazing!

2476
01:11:48,240 --> 01:11:49,880
The emperor's horse really is different!

2477
01:11:52,880 --> 01:11:54,440
Feels like we've left the group behind.

2478
01:11:54,440 --> 01:11:55,720
Like we're galloping across the plains.

2479
01:11:56,000 --> 01:11:56,880
Are you brave enough?

2480
01:11:56,880 --> 01:11:57,400
Be honest.

2481
01:11:57,400 --> 01:11:58,880
I'm brave when I'm with you.

2482
01:11:59,080 --> 01:12:00,800
I'm brave when I'm with you.

2483
01:12:03,140 --> 01:12:03,980
(Speeds up)

2484
01:12:04,000 --> 01:12:05,560
Just yell "jiu" and it'll run!

2485
01:12:16,200 --> 01:12:17,480
Xing, you're amazing!

2486
01:12:24,280 --> 01:12:25,440
Xing knows how to ride!

2487
01:12:26,280 --> 01:12:27,160
She's riding up front,

2488
01:12:27,160 --> 01:12:28,120
like a princess!

2489
01:12:31,590 --> 01:12:32,140
Let's go!

2490
01:12:47,400 --> 01:12:49,280
It's so peaceful over here!

2491
01:12:49,280 --> 01:12:50,400
Yeah!

2492
01:12:50,840 --> 01:12:52,200
We feel like the parents.

2493
01:12:52,440 --> 01:12:54,280
Look how energetic the kids are!

2494
01:12:55,880 --> 01:12:57,000
It's fine. We'll just take it easy.

2495
01:12:57,270 --> 01:12:58,880
Dai Xu and I

2496
01:12:58,880 --> 01:12:59,880
are doing just fine.

2497
01:13:00,960 --> 01:13:01,840
Nice.

2498
01:13:05,140 --> 01:13:06,380
(Bonfire dinner campsite)

2499
01:13:06,400 --> 01:13:07,080
We're here.

2500
01:13:07,680 --> 01:13:08,160
Let's go!

2501
01:13:10,240 --> 01:13:11,720
I can already smell the fire.

2502
01:13:11,720 --> 01:13:12,320
They're dancing.

2503
01:13:16,480 --> 01:13:17,280
So beautiful!

2504
01:13:17,300 --> 01:13:19,020
(Dancing to the beat)

2505
01:13:24,800 --> 01:13:25,640
Wishing you good fortune!

2506
01:13:25,640 --> 01:13:27,040
Thank you!

2507
01:13:27,480 --> 01:13:28,560
Welcome to Inner Mongolia!

2508
01:13:28,560 --> 01:13:29,360
Thank you!

2509
01:13:30,600 --> 01:13:31,400
Thanks!

2510
01:13:32,040 --> 01:13:33,080
This color goes so well

2511
01:13:33,080 --> 01:13:33,920
with my outfit.

2512
01:13:34,120 --> 01:13:34,800
They're all shades of blue.

2513
01:13:36,760 --> 01:13:37,480
Thanks!

2514
01:13:37,480 --> 01:13:38,320
Okay, thank you!

2515
01:13:38,320 --> 01:13:39,840
Let me pull your hair out.

2516
01:13:39,960 --> 01:13:40,720
I want roasted lamb!

2517
01:13:41,680 --> 01:13:43,000
Time for some delicious food!

2518
01:13:43,760 --> 01:13:44,560
Yummy food!

2519
01:13:46,280 --> 01:13:47,240
Smells amazing!

2520
01:13:47,640 --> 01:13:48,240
Have a seat anywhere.

2521
01:13:48,240 --> 01:13:48,760
Anywhere you like.

2522
01:13:50,440 --> 01:13:51,080
Come here, Xiaoyu!

2523
01:13:51,080 --> 01:13:51,960
Come on, Xiaoyu!

2524
01:13:51,960 --> 01:13:52,880
I'll sit next to you two.

2525
01:13:52,880 --> 01:13:53,440
Okay!

2526
01:13:53,800 --> 01:13:54,240
So lucky!

2527
01:13:54,520 --> 01:13:55,320
I'll sit next to you guys.

2528
01:13:55,430 --> 01:13:56,600
(Everyone takes their seats)
Alright.

2529
01:13:56,600 --> 01:13:58,040
Well, my dear friends,

2530
01:13:58,040 --> 01:13:59,080
let's dig in!

2531
01:14:03,720 --> 01:14:05,040
Let's carve up this lamb.

2532
01:14:05,040 --> 01:14:06,280
All the men, come over!

2533
01:14:06,880 --> 01:14:08,000
The men of each family?

2534
01:14:08,000 --> 01:14:08,360
Yeah.

2535
01:14:08,360 --> 01:14:08,800
Our family...

2536
01:14:08,800 --> 01:14:09,960
Do we count?

2537
01:14:09,960 --> 01:14:10,940
(Caught off guard)
We do, right?

2538
01:14:11,280 --> 01:14:12,200
I'll get some for you two.

2539
01:14:12,200 --> 01:14:13,000
You two stay seated.

2540
01:14:13,000 --> 01:14:14,480
You always looked after everyone
in the house.

2541
01:14:15,040 --> 01:14:16,200
Let me take care of you today.

2542
01:14:16,200 --> 01:14:16,640
How sweet!

2543
01:14:16,640 --> 01:14:17,800
Meng, how sweet!

2544
01:14:21,560 --> 01:14:22,160
Here, quick!

2545
01:14:22,560 --> 01:14:24,600
Here you go!

2546
01:14:24,600 --> 01:14:25,480
Thanks!

2547
01:14:26,000 --> 01:14:26,800
Here it comes!

2548
01:14:26,980 --> 01:14:27,720
Wow!

2549
01:14:28,320 --> 01:14:29,120
Amazing!

2550
01:14:30,960 --> 01:14:32,080
This tastes pretty good. Try it.

2551
01:14:32,560 --> 01:14:33,400
This sweet potato's not bad.

2552
01:14:33,400 --> 01:14:35,000
Grab it with your other hand.

2553
01:14:35,960 --> 01:14:37,400
Open wide.

2554
01:14:38,120 --> 01:14:38,920
Try it.

2555
01:14:40,280 --> 01:14:41,280
Is this sweet potato?

2556
01:14:42,040 --> 01:14:43,080
I don't think it is.

2557
01:14:43,080 --> 01:14:44,080
But it's good.

2558
01:14:44,920 --> 01:14:45,680
Eat up.

2559
01:14:46,120 --> 01:14:47,080
This lamb's delicious!

2560
01:14:47,280 --> 01:14:48,600
Better than any I've had before!

2561
01:14:49,160 --> 01:14:50,280
This lamb's really good!

2562
01:14:50,280 --> 01:14:51,520
Skewers. Haitao,

2563
01:14:51,520 --> 01:14:52,320
Chaoyue, have some.

2564
01:14:52,320 --> 01:14:52,960
It's fine. Don't worry about us.

2565
01:14:52,960 --> 01:14:53,400
Don't!

2566
01:14:53,400 --> 01:14:54,000
Just eat your own food.

2567
01:14:54,000 --> 01:14:54,840
But they can't reach.

2568
01:14:54,840 --> 01:14:55,600
Don't they have some over there?

2569
01:14:55,600 --> 01:14:56,280
Chen Hewen!

2570
01:14:57,920 --> 01:14:59,000
You don't have to look after everyone.

2571
01:14:59,000 --> 01:15:00,000
Just look after yourself!

2572
01:15:00,000 --> 01:15:00,800
Got it!

2573
01:15:02,360 --> 01:15:03,360
Exactly! That's today's lesson.

2574
01:15:03,840 --> 01:15:05,080
Why are you fussing over everyone again?

2575
01:15:05,320 --> 01:15:06,600
Just tell us what you want to eat.

2576
01:15:06,760 --> 01:15:07,560
Okay!

2577
01:15:08,840 --> 01:15:10,120
This whole plate's yours.

2578
01:15:10,560 --> 01:15:11,240
Get me a skewer.

2579
01:15:11,440 --> 01:15:12,400
I'm not looking after you guys anymore.

2580
01:15:13,840 --> 01:15:14,480
This is ours.

2581
01:15:14,480 --> 01:15:15,320
That's how you do it, see?

2582
01:15:15,320 --> 01:15:16,380
(Putting the lesson into practice)
Bring it back!

2583
01:15:18,440 --> 01:15:19,160
Here you go!

2584
01:15:19,820 --> 01:15:21,260
(Joking around)

2585
01:15:21,400 --> 01:15:23,400
When the show was airing,

2586
01:15:24,200 --> 01:15:25,400
you all went online, right?

2587
01:15:33,280 --> 01:15:34,480
I think our relationship

2588
01:15:34,480 --> 01:15:36,320
with the viewers is about

2589
01:15:36,320 --> 01:15:37,200
being there for each other.

2590
01:15:38,080 --> 01:15:38,880
Because

2591
01:15:38,880 --> 01:15:41,880
we've shared so many genuine feelings.

2592
01:15:42,040 --> 01:15:42,640
And the viewers

2593
01:15:42,640 --> 01:15:45,240
have poured even more love

2594
01:15:45,240 --> 01:15:46,120
into supporting us.

2595
01:15:46,480 --> 01:15:47,720
Have you guys seen what people

2596
01:15:47,720 --> 01:15:49,000
are saying about you online?

2597
01:15:56,120 --> 01:15:57,040
I have.

2598
01:15:57,040 --> 01:15:58,280
They call me

2599
01:15:58,280 --> 01:15:59,320
the Lucky Guy.

2600
01:16:01,720 --> 01:16:02,640
The Lucky Guy?

2601
01:16:02,640 --> 01:16:03,280
Yeah.

2602
01:16:03,280 --> 01:16:04,680
Do you think you're lucky?

2603
01:16:05,820 --> 01:16:07,060
(All ears)

2604
01:16:07,520 --> 01:16:09,480
I think it's pretty funny.

2605
01:16:09,920 --> 01:16:11,720
The way people tease me online

2606
01:16:11,720 --> 01:16:13,160
is actually pretty entertaining.

2607
01:16:13,680 --> 01:16:14,400
I do think

2608
01:16:14,400 --> 01:16:15,360
I'm pretty lucky,

2609
01:16:15,360 --> 01:16:17,520
having met Xing.

2610
01:16:17,520 --> 01:16:18,120
Yeah.

2611
01:16:23,680 --> 01:16:25,800
Everyone says you spoil Bohan.

2612
01:16:25,880 --> 01:16:26,720
Is that true, Xing?

2613
01:16:26,720 --> 01:16:28,140
(Curious)

2614
01:16:30,200 --> 01:16:31,880
I really do spoil you, right?

2615
01:16:32,560 --> 01:16:33,040
Yeah.

2616
01:16:35,960 --> 01:16:37,320
You like hearing him ramble.

2617
01:16:37,960 --> 01:16:39,240
It feels weird when he's quiet.

2618
01:16:43,120 --> 01:16:44,000
She doesn't find me annoying.

2619
01:16:44,000 --> 01:16:44,880
That's pretty great.

2620
01:16:47,220 --> 01:16:48,660
(Getting a dose of PDA)

2621
01:16:48,700 --> 01:16:49,780
(So natural)

2622
01:16:49,820 --> 01:16:51,060
(Everyone's watching)

2623
01:16:53,520 --> 01:16:54,160
Careful!

2624
01:16:54,160 --> 01:16:54,960
It's fine, Fang.

2625
01:16:55,040 --> 01:16:56,360
So in love you can't feel pain, huh?

2626
01:16:58,960 --> 01:17:00,120
Which of you cries more easily?

2627
01:17:00,520 --> 01:17:01,560
Dai Xu's the perfect person

2628
01:17:01,560 --> 01:17:02,680
to ask this question.

2629
01:17:02,940 --> 01:17:04,140
(Fellow crybabies)

2630
01:17:04,880 --> 01:17:06,080
Dai Xu's a little crybaby too.

2631
01:17:06,080 --> 01:17:06,980
(Let's be real)
Drop the "little"!

2632
01:17:07,140 --> 01:17:08,420
(Big crybaby and little crybaby)

2633
01:17:09,160 --> 01:17:10,440
Before I met Xing,

2634
01:17:10,440 --> 01:17:11,880
I hardly ever cried.

2635
01:17:12,080 --> 01:17:13,400
It's been years since

2636
01:17:13,400 --> 01:17:14,880
I've cried as much

2637
01:17:14,880 --> 01:17:17,480
as I have lately.

2638
01:17:17,480 --> 01:17:18,600
Maybe you just forgot.

2639
01:17:19,080 --> 01:17:19,640
No.

2640
01:17:19,640 --> 01:17:20,280
Seriously.

2641
01:17:21,280 --> 01:17:22,080
I guess

2642
01:17:22,080 --> 01:17:24,560
her emotions have rubbed off on me.

2643
01:17:27,600 --> 01:17:28,120
Yeah.

2644
01:17:29,040 --> 01:17:30,240
What do you think, Xing?

2645
01:17:30,560 --> 01:17:32,480
The last time we cried was

2646
01:17:32,480 --> 01:17:33,600
during the watch-along.

2647
01:17:33,800 --> 01:17:34,680
It was when he came

2648
01:17:35,040 --> 01:17:36,400
to see me at the hospital.

2649
01:17:36,400 --> 01:17:37,600
Something just hit us.

2650
01:17:37,600 --> 01:17:39,040
We both started crying at once.

2651
01:17:40,160 --> 01:17:42,040
That was a really tough time.

2652
01:17:49,920 --> 01:17:50,720
She's crying?

2653
01:17:51,080 --> 01:17:51,960
No, she's eating.

2654
01:17:53,360 --> 01:17:54,600
Let her say something!

2655
01:17:54,660 --> 01:17:56,260
(Too loved to speak)

2656
01:17:58,720 --> 01:17:59,720
Sha Yue'er, Zhao Xilun!

2657
01:18:01,540 --> 01:18:02,900
(What's up?)

2658
01:18:02,920 --> 01:18:04,440
I'll just say what's on my mind.

2659
01:18:04,580 --> 01:18:05,480
(Speak your mind)

2660
01:18:05,480 --> 01:18:06,160
Well...

2661
01:18:11,680 --> 01:18:13,160
They call me an empty shell,

2662
01:18:13,160 --> 01:18:15,160
complicated,
and a flower without fragrance.

2663
01:18:18,120 --> 01:18:20,040
You actually said those out loud!

2664
01:18:20,040 --> 01:18:20,880
I mean...

2665
01:18:20,880 --> 01:18:22,160
Even if that were in my script,

2666
01:18:22,160 --> 01:18:22,840
I wouldn't say it!

2667
01:18:24,940 --> 01:18:25,800
(Comforts her)

2668
01:18:25,800 --> 01:18:27,240
How did you feel

2669
01:18:27,240 --> 01:18:28,080
when you first saw those comments?

2670
01:18:29,840 --> 01:18:31,720
At least they think I'm pretty.

2671
01:18:35,320 --> 01:18:35,720
Nice!

2672
01:18:35,720 --> 01:18:37,080
I love that attitude!

2673
01:18:37,080 --> 01:18:37,760
They're right!

2674
01:18:38,600 --> 01:18:39,720
I really do

2675
01:18:40,800 --> 01:18:41,680
overthink things.

2676
01:18:41,680 --> 01:18:43,680
And I tend to make things complicated.

2677
01:18:45,720 --> 01:18:46,520
But...

2678
01:18:48,000 --> 01:18:49,760
Zhao Xilun

2679
01:18:50,800 --> 01:18:52,960
helps me work through all that.

2680
01:18:54,160 --> 01:18:56,920
Even when we

2681
01:18:56,920 --> 01:18:58,280
have disagreements,

2682
01:18:58,280 --> 01:19:00,560
I feel like he always makes sure

2683
01:19:01,600 --> 01:19:03,280
I'm okay emotionally

2684
01:19:03,280 --> 01:19:04,240
before talking things through.

2685
01:19:06,600 --> 01:19:07,640
Yue'er just

2686
01:19:07,640 --> 01:19:08,520
overthinks a lot.

2687
01:19:10,680 --> 01:19:12,280
But deep down,

2688
01:19:12,280 --> 01:19:13,560
she's really kindhearted.

2689
01:19:13,920 --> 01:19:14,920
She just doesn't know what to do.

2690
01:19:15,800 --> 01:19:17,120
When things get stressful,

2691
01:19:17,280 --> 01:19:17,760
especially

2692
01:19:17,760 --> 01:19:19,200
under so much pressure,

2693
01:19:20,120 --> 01:19:20,650
you just

2694
01:19:21,040 --> 01:19:23,240
need to give yourself some space.

2695
01:19:27,280 --> 01:19:28,680
Let people say what they want.

2696
01:19:28,680 --> 01:19:30,200
Our feelings are real anyway.

2697
01:19:31,280 --> 01:19:32,080
Exactly!

2698
01:19:35,960 --> 01:19:36,960
But you all know

2699
01:19:36,960 --> 01:19:38,240
that being on this show

2700
01:19:38,480 --> 01:19:39,760
means

2701
01:19:39,760 --> 01:19:41,320
more people will pay attention to you.

2702
01:19:42,200 --> 01:19:43,040
And it's not just you.

2703
01:19:43,040 --> 01:19:44,800
Even we still hear

2704
01:19:44,800 --> 01:19:46,440
all kinds of opinions.

2705
01:19:46,440 --> 01:19:47,840
So I think

2706
01:19:47,920 --> 01:19:48,840
through it all,

2707
01:19:48,960 --> 01:19:50,960
we need to take good care

2708
01:19:50,960 --> 01:19:51,920
of each other.

2709
01:19:52,760 --> 01:19:54,280
Protect what you have together.

2710
01:19:54,280 --> 01:19:55,600
That's what matters most, okay?

2711
01:19:55,840 --> 01:19:56,560
Yeah.

2712
01:19:56,560 --> 01:19:57,480
That goes for every couple.

2713
01:19:57,800 --> 01:19:58,600
Thank you.

2714
01:20:01,880 --> 01:20:02,320
Si!

2715
01:20:03,760 --> 01:20:04,840
Was the crispy sweet-and-sour pork good?

2716
01:20:04,860 --> 01:20:06,100
(Asking her on the spot)

2717
01:20:06,400 --> 01:20:07,240
Delicious.

2718
01:20:07,660 --> 01:20:08,780
(Triple confusion)

2719
01:20:09,040 --> 01:20:09,600
I wasn't asking you!

2720
01:20:10,720 --> 01:20:11,760
I asked Si!

2721
01:20:12,000 --> 01:20:12,960
It was really good.

2722
01:20:12,960 --> 01:20:13,640
Really?

2723
01:20:13,640 --> 01:20:14,120
Yeah.

2724
01:20:14,120 --> 01:20:16,200
Better than what restaurants make.

2725
01:20:20,160 --> 01:20:21,400
Since that meal,

2726
01:20:21,400 --> 01:20:22,400
have you tried

2727
01:20:22,400 --> 01:20:23,720
anything else he's cooked?

2728
01:20:24,400 --> 01:20:25,360
Chicken curry.

2729
01:20:25,360 --> 01:20:25,760
Yeah.

2730
01:20:25,760 --> 01:20:27,240
He made chicken curry recently.

2731
01:20:28,640 --> 01:20:29,400
And noodles.

2732
01:20:29,400 --> 01:20:30,120
Right, noodles too.

2733
01:20:30,120 --> 01:20:30,920
All really good.

2734
01:20:30,920 --> 01:20:31,520
Army stew.

2735
01:20:31,760 --> 01:20:33,360
Cui Yihang keeps reminding her!

2736
01:20:33,880 --> 01:20:34,840
(Caught red-handed)
I don't want her to forget!

2737
01:20:34,840 --> 01:20:35,360
In case she forgets.

2738
01:20:36,600 --> 01:20:37,920
Did you really make all that?

2739
01:20:37,920 --> 01:20:38,600
Seriously.

2740
01:20:38,600 --> 01:20:39,120
He did.

2741
01:20:39,320 --> 01:20:40,200
Where'd you cook it?

2742
01:20:40,200 --> 01:20:40,700
(Tries a different question)

2743
01:20:40,940 --> 01:20:41,820
(Exactly what I wanted to ask)

2744
01:20:43,000 --> 01:20:43,800
At...

2745
01:20:44,400 --> 01:20:44,680
Okay!

2746
01:20:44,680 --> 01:20:45,480
Never mind!

2747
01:20:48,400 --> 01:20:49,400
What's the latest gift

2748
01:20:49,400 --> 01:20:50,400
you gave Si?

2749
01:20:51,000 --> 01:20:51,880
A dinnerware set.

2750
01:20:51,880 --> 01:20:53,280
Plates and bowls,

2751
01:20:53,280 --> 01:20:54,520
cups and stuff.

2752
01:20:54,640 --> 01:20:56,120
One set or a matching pair?

2753
01:20:59,280 --> 01:20:59,840
One set.

2754
01:20:59,840 --> 01:21:01,320
We can both use the same set.

2755
01:21:02,120 --> 01:21:02,800
One set for two?

2756
01:21:02,800 --> 01:21:04,680
So you eat together all the time?

2757
01:21:04,720 --> 01:21:05,360
Yeah.

2758
01:21:05,920 --> 01:21:06,520
Wait, no!

2759
01:21:06,760 --> 01:21:07,880
No!

2760
01:21:11,560 --> 01:21:13,160
No!

2761
01:21:13,520 --> 01:21:14,840
I didn't catch that.

2762
01:21:14,840 --> 01:21:15,640
What was that, Jingke?

2763
01:21:16,000 --> 01:21:17,120
Never mind.

2764
01:21:17,120 --> 01:21:18,040
We're done asking.

2765
01:21:20,300 --> 01:21:20,880
Chen Hewen!

2766
01:21:21,600 --> 01:21:22,520
I've noticed you sometimes

2767
01:21:22,520 --> 01:21:24,120
go to your room and write things down.

2768
01:21:24,320 --> 01:21:25,280
Yeah, that's...

2769
01:21:25,280 --> 01:21:26,360
What do you write?

2770
01:21:26,380 --> 01:21:27,500
(Curious)

2771
01:21:28,760 --> 01:21:29,760
Well...

2772
01:21:30,920 --> 01:21:32,600
I wrote down everyone's

2773
01:21:33,480 --> 01:21:34,040
like,

2774
01:21:34,040 --> 01:21:34,920
personality types.

2775
01:21:35,040 --> 01:21:35,720
And

2776
01:21:35,720 --> 01:21:37,240
birthdays and interests.

2777
01:21:38,040 --> 01:21:39,400
Even favorite colors.

2778
01:21:39,960 --> 01:21:41,040
Doing background checks, huh?

2779
01:21:41,920 --> 01:21:42,800
Early on,

2780
01:21:42,800 --> 01:21:43,880
I didn't know everyone well.

2781
01:21:43,880 --> 01:21:45,400
I wanted to get to know them faster,

2782
01:21:45,400 --> 01:21:46,400
so I took notes.

2783
01:21:47,200 --> 01:21:48,360
Like a little journal.

2784
01:21:49,240 --> 01:21:50,480
The quiet observer.

2785
01:21:51,200 --> 01:21:51,680
Yeah.

2786
01:21:53,960 --> 01:21:54,760
Meng!

2787
01:21:55,800 --> 01:21:56,600
Meng!

2788
01:21:57,440 --> 01:21:59,720
Where do you get

2789
01:21:59,720 --> 01:22:00,760
all your energy?

2790
01:22:00,760 --> 01:22:01,260
(Curious)

2791
01:22:04,520 --> 01:22:05,440
Actually,

2792
01:22:05,440 --> 01:22:06,520
on my way to the Signal House,

2793
01:22:06,520 --> 01:22:07,760
I'd be passed out the whole way.

2794
01:22:08,790 --> 01:22:09,840
But once I walked in

2795
01:22:09,840 --> 01:22:11,160
and saw anyone,

2796
01:22:11,160 --> 01:22:11,600
I'd just

2797
01:22:12,000 --> 01:22:13,200
wake right up.

2798
01:22:14,360 --> 01:22:16,720
They give me energy.

2799
01:22:21,100 --> 01:22:21,980
(Turns around)

2800
01:22:22,200 --> 01:22:23,880
Do you live far apart in Tianjin?

2801
01:22:23,880 --> 01:22:24,640
(Straight to the questions)
Not far.

2802
01:22:24,640 --> 01:22:25,120
Not far.

2803
01:22:25,120 --> 01:22:26,320
What's your age gap?

2804
01:22:26,680 --> 01:22:27,920
One year.

2805
01:22:27,920 --> 01:22:29,040
What middle and high schools

2806
01:22:29,040 --> 01:22:30,280
did you go to? Have you checked?

2807
01:22:30,280 --> 01:22:31,720
Yeah. We never crossed paths.

2808
01:22:32,220 --> 01:22:33,740
(Fishing for details fails)

2809
01:22:35,040 --> 01:22:36,640
So it's all thanks to the show!

2810
01:22:36,800 --> 01:22:38,440
Thank you, Heart Signal!

2811
01:22:41,200 --> 01:22:43,000
I saw another comment saying,

2812
01:22:43,280 --> 01:22:44,960
"Cao Yiheng, ease up on the sweet talk!"

2813
01:22:44,960 --> 01:22:46,040
"Cui Kaiyi's still young!"

2814
01:22:52,040 --> 01:22:53,440
Well...

2815
01:22:54,000 --> 01:22:56,360
it's just that

2816
01:22:56,360 --> 01:22:57,840
my feelings at the time

2817
01:22:57,840 --> 01:22:59,720
were that strong.

2818
01:23:01,680 --> 01:23:02,520
Normally,

2819
01:23:02,520 --> 01:23:04,400
if you asked me
to say something romantic,

2820
01:23:04,400 --> 01:23:05,320
I couldn't do it.

2821
01:23:06,240 --> 01:23:07,840
I think Cui Kaiyi brought it

2822
01:23:07,840 --> 01:23:08,360
out of me.

2823
01:23:08,680 --> 01:23:09,640
You were swept up in love.

2824
01:23:09,720 --> 01:23:10,440
Exactly.

2825
01:23:10,450 --> 01:23:12,000
So which of Cao Yiheng's words

2826
01:23:12,000 --> 01:23:12,800
made your heart flutter most?

2827
01:23:17,440 --> 01:23:19,120
He doesn't need to speak.
Just seeing him does it!

2828
01:23:20,880 --> 01:23:21,680
Let me think.

2829
01:23:23,240 --> 01:23:24,520
Or did he ever say something

2830
01:23:24,520 --> 01:23:26,360
you never expected to hear?

2831
01:23:27,480 --> 01:23:30,560
He once told me

2832
01:23:30,560 --> 01:23:32,440
he'd been alone in a little house,

2833
01:23:32,440 --> 01:23:34,760
and I was the one making noise outside

2834
01:23:34,760 --> 01:23:36,360
who pulled him out of his room.

2835
01:23:42,600 --> 01:23:43,240
Xiaoyu,

2836
01:23:44,360 --> 01:23:44,920
before the show,

2837
01:23:44,920 --> 01:23:46,680
did you know you were this funny?

2838
01:23:48,120 --> 01:23:49,200
Actually,

2839
01:23:49,760 --> 01:23:51,890
I've always been like this off-camera.

2840
01:23:51,920 --> 01:23:52,800
A funny girl, huh?

2841
01:23:53,480 --> 01:23:54,040
Yeah.

2842
01:23:54,600 --> 01:23:56,320
I loved watching comedies as a kid.

2843
01:23:57,520 --> 01:24:00,400
So sometimes when I'm talking,

2844
01:24:00,400 --> 01:24:02,720
I'll randomly quote comedy lines.

2845
01:24:03,480 --> 01:24:04,360
Yeah.

2846
01:24:06,680 --> 01:24:08,760
I did plenty
of weird stuff in the house.

2847
01:24:08,760 --> 01:24:10,040
Meng can tell you all about it.

2848
01:24:10,660 --> 01:24:12,020
(All ears)

2849
01:24:12,560 --> 01:24:13,920
But seriously,

2850
01:24:14,640 --> 01:24:16,600
she has such a funny side.

2851
01:24:16,600 --> 01:24:18,800
Even more so in real life.

2852
01:24:19,280 --> 01:24:20,280
At first, Meng

2853
01:24:20,280 --> 01:24:21,160
said I was

2854
01:24:21,520 --> 01:24:22,840
super intellectual

2855
01:24:23,000 --> 01:24:24,000
and logical.

2856
01:24:24,480 --> 01:24:25,360
Yeah, but then she realized

2857
01:24:25,360 --> 01:24:26,560
that's not really me.

2858
01:24:26,840 --> 01:24:28,400
Actually, when we watched the show,

2859
01:24:28,400 --> 01:24:29,720
every time it cut to The Courageous,

2860
01:24:29,720 --> 01:24:31,240
we called it The Courageous' room.

2861
01:24:31,480 --> 01:24:32,720
And every time you appeared,

2862
01:24:32,720 --> 01:24:34,440
you were always in the same position.

2863
01:24:34,440 --> 01:24:35,120
On your bed,

2864
01:24:35,120 --> 01:24:36,160
you'd be like this.

2865
01:24:36,160 --> 01:24:36,800
Just like this!

2866
01:24:41,920 --> 01:24:42,520
Ouch!

2867
01:24:42,800 --> 01:24:43,200
Sorry!

2868
01:24:43,440 --> 01:24:43,960
Dai Xu!

2869
01:24:43,960 --> 01:24:44,400
Where'd he go?

2870
01:24:44,800 --> 01:24:45,840
Sorry!

2871
01:24:46,160 --> 01:24:47,560
It's fine. Cut this part out!

2872
01:24:49,560 --> 01:24:50,480
Got too excited.

2873
01:24:50,640 --> 01:24:50,920
Yeah.

2874
01:24:50,920 --> 01:24:52,040
I don't even know why I...

2875
01:24:52,320 --> 01:24:52,760
You're

2876
01:24:52,760 --> 01:24:53,800
always

2877
01:24:53,800 --> 01:24:54,600
lying like this!

2878
01:24:54,600 --> 01:24:55,640
And every time,

2879
01:24:55,640 --> 01:24:57,280
